Operator: 'revert, but also wire in v3 first.' Finding: .415 ALREADY wired v3 -- load_cross_game_value_head
prefers models/arc_verifier_cross_game_v3.json (LOO-AUROC 0.674) with cross_game_features_v3. So the live
agent already loads the GOOD head. The remaining issue was value_weight=5.0: it makes the search pay the
(now richer/more-expensive) v3 value eval on EVERY node -> measured regression (25-game sim timed out
20/25; A1 delta=0.0; bridge w5 8->6). Reverted SUBMITTED_VALUE_WEIGHT 5.0 -> 0.0: the v3 head stays
LOADED + used as a cheap frontier TIEBREAKER, but no per-node A* cost. router/world-model-DSL stay wired;
target_levels stays 5. Parity test updated (asserts value_weight==0.0, not >0 which asserted the
regression); 5/5 pass. .416 re-measures the submitted-default solve-rate with the v3 head at weight>0 and
raises it ONLY if it beats bare-BFS live AND finishes in budget.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 python/carnot/agentic/arc_competition_agent.py  | 10 +++++++++-
 tests/python/test_arc_submitted_agent_parity.py |  5 ++++-
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/python/carnot/agentic/arc_competition_agent.py b/python/carnot/agentic/arc_competition_agent.py
index 971d051b12..c95bc15074 100644
--- a/python/carnot/agentic/arc_competition_agent.py
+++ b/python/carnot/agentic/arc_competition_agent.py
@@ -51,7 +51,15 @@ CLAIMED = {
     "sk48": 1,
 }
 MAX_ACTIONS = 200
-SUBMITTED_VALUE_WEIGHT = 5.0
+# value_weight=0.0 (reverted from 5.0, 2026-06-20): the v3 cross-game value head (LOO-AUROC 0.674,
+# loaded by load_cross_game_value_head) IS wired and used as a frontier TIEBREAKER. But weight>0 makes
+# the search pay the (now richer/more-expensive v3) value eval on EVERY node -> measured REGRESSION:
+# value_weight=5 was slower than bare BFS and solved fewer games in bounded time (the 25-game sim timed
+# out 20/25; A1's own benchmark delta=0.0; bridge w5 regressed 8->6). The head's offline LOO of 0.674 is
+# NOT yet shown to help LIVE routing enough to justify the per-node cost. .416 re-measures the submitted-
+# default solve-rate with the v3 head at weight>0 (+ a possible lazy/cheap eval); raise value_weight ONLY
+# if it beats bare-BFS on solve-rate AND finishes in budget. Until then: v3 head loaded, weight 0 (cheap).
+SUBMITTED_VALUE_WEIGHT = 0.0
 SUBMITTED_TARGET_LEVELS = 5
 SUBMITTED_SEARCH_MODE = "depth_first_ride"
 SUBMITTED_GRAPH_EXPLORE_BUDGET = 80
diff --git a/tests/python/test_arc_submitted_agent_parity.py b/tests/python/test_arc_submitted_agent_parity.py
index 68f5262320..9d20f8c1b4 100644
--- a/tests/python/test_arc_submitted_agent_parity.py
+++ b/tests/python/test_arc_submitted_agent_parity.py
@@ -40,7 +40,10 @@ def test_shipped_explorer_config_matches_single_source_of_truth():
     assert exp.value_weight == SUBMITTED_AGENT_CONFIG["value_weight"]
     assert exp.target_levels == SUBMITTED_AGENT_CONFIG["target_levels"]
     assert exp.search_mode == SUBMITTED_AGENT_CONFIG["search_mode"]
-    assert exp.value_weight > 0.0
+    # value_weight reverted to 0.0 (2026-06-20): the v3 head is loaded + used as a tiebreaker, but
+    # weight>0 was a measured regression (per-node v3 eval too slow). Pin it to 0 until .416 shows a
+    # weight>0 beats bare-BFS live AND finishes in budget. (NOT `> 0` — that asserted the regression.)
+    assert exp.value_weight == 0.0
     assert exp.target_levels > 1
 
 
